course: dictionary
lesson: 13032
title: Fallible: able to make mistakes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fallible is a long word, but its meaning is simple: it means able to make mistakes or be wrong. Look for clues around it, just as you would for any new word.
explain: «Everyone is fallible, even the best teacher.» The clue is «even the best»: the sentence says that all people can make mistakes, including the best teachers.
explain: «My memory is fallible, so I write my shopping list down.» The clue is «so I write it down». The speaker knows their memory can be wrong, so they check it with a list.
explain: Fallible is the opposite of infallible, which means never wrong. Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Everyone is able to make mistakes, even the best teacher.» If it still makes sense, you have it.
fact: Fallible means able to make mistakes or be wrong.
fact: «Fallible» is an adjective; «fallibility» is the noun for the quality of being fallible.
fact: The opposite of fallible is infallible, which means never wrong.
fact: «Fallible» things, like memory or tests, are not always reliable.
fact: Everyone is fallible, even experts and machines, so we check our work and accept that others can make mistakes.
exercise: «The map was fallible, so we checked the road signs too.» What does fallible mean here? | Brand new and shiny | *Able to make mistakes or be wrong | Always right, so no checking is needed | Very large and heavy
exercise: Which word is the opposite of fallible? | Brave | *Infallible | Careless | Tired
exercise: «Even the best scientists are fallible.» Why does the author say this? | Because they are always the tallest in the room | Because they never make mistakes | *Because they can make mistakes too | Because they only work at night
test: «My fallible memory forgot my PE kit again.» What does fallible tell you about the memory? | It is made of metal | It is always perfect | It is very loud | *It can be wrong or forget things
test: Which sentence shows fallibility best? | I never check anything because I am always right | Nobody makes mistakes, ever | Machines are never wrong, so we never test them | *Everyone makes mistakes, so I check my spelling
exam: Mia says, «Teachers are fallible.» What does Mia mean? | Teachers are very tall | *Teachers can sometimes be wrong | Teachers are never wrong | Teachers only teach on Mondays
